{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"correct-by-construction-parsing","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"Correct-by-Construction Parsing"}]},"title_text":"Correct-by-Construction Parsing","kind":"note","taxon":null,"url":"correct-by-construction-parsing.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"entry","attrs":[["entry","correct-by-construction-parsing"],["kind","note"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Parsers are some of the most important pieces of software that we have. You have likely relied on "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"dozens"}]},{"Text":" of parsers to even read this message. Anytime someone writes a piece of high-level code, it must be "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"parsed"}]},{"Text":" into a representation that is workable for the machine."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Because parsers are so ubiquituous, the correctness of so many other programs is contingent on a bug-free parser. Despite this fundamental reliance, parsers are often "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"unverified"}]},{"Text":". Buggy parsers have led to many critical security vulnerabilities. Even in otherwise verified software development, parsing is usually unverified (or the final component to become verified)."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"To address this gap, we develop Lambek"},{"Math":{"src":"\"\"^mono(D)"}},{"Text":", a domain-specific programming language for writing "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"intrinsically correct"}]},{"Text":" parsers. That is, if a parser written in Lambek"},{"Math":{"src":"\"\"^mono(D)"}},{"Text":" compiles then we guarantee the resulting program is sound with respect to its parsing semantics."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"I first explored this idea in "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"intrinsic-verification-of-parsers","label":null,"body":null}},{"Text":", and it will be the focus of my dissertation."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Notes and sketches of ongoing work in Lambek"},{"Math":{"src":"\"\"^mono(D)"}},{"Text":" may be found below and throughout this site."}]},{"Group":{"role":"query","attrs":[["collapsible","true"],["open","false"],["summary","30 entries"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"query-item","attrs":[["entry","day-quotient"],["date","20261001"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Transclude":{"id":"day-quotient","opts":{"expanded":false,"numbered":true,"title":"Auto","level":null,"section":false}}}]}}},{"Group":{"role":"query-item","attrs":[["entry","dependent-tensor"],["date","20261001"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Transclude":{"id":"dependent-tensor","opts":{"expanded":false,"numbered":true,"title":"Auto","level":null,"section":false}}}]}}},{"Group":{"role":"query-item","attrs":[["entry","formal-grammar"],["date","20261001"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Transclude":{"id":"formal-grammar","opts":{"expanded":false,"numbered":true,"title":"Auto","level":null,"section":false}}}]}}},{"Group":{"role":"query-item","attrs":[["entry","grammar-quotients"],["date","20261001"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Transclude":{"id":"grammar-quotients","opts":{"expanded":false,"numbered":true,"title":"Auto","level":null,"section":false}}}]}}},{"Group":{"role":"query-item","attrs":[["entry","grammar-residual"],["date","20261001"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Transclude":{"id":"grammar-residual","opts":{"expanded":false,"numbered":true,"title":"Auto","level":null,"section":false}}}]}}},{"Group":{"role":"query-item","attrs":[["entry","grammar-tensor"],["date","20261001"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Transclude":{"id":"grammar-tensor","opts":{"expanded":false,"numbered":true,"title":"Auto","level":null,"section":false}}}]}}},{"Group":{"role":"query-item","attrs":[["entry","theory-type"],["date","20260929"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Transclude":{"id":"theory-type","opts":{"expanded":false,"numbered":true,"title":"Auto","level":null,"section":false}}}]}}},{"Group":{"role":"query-item","attrs":[["entry","representable-grammar"],["date","20260824"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Transclude":{"id":"representable-grammar","opts":{"expanded":false,"numbered":true,"title":"Auto","level":null,"section":false}}}]}}},{"Group":{"role":"query-item","attrs":[["entry